## Per-backend OBO identity tests (Delta / Lakebase / Neo4j)

Context:
Locked the OBO identity split at the backend-construction layer so the contract
can't silently change: Delta/Lakehouse reads run on-behalf-of the caller, while
Lakebase Postgres and Neo4j stay on the service principal / stored Bolt profile
and never consult the request identity (they are gated at the endpoint by Team
membership instead).

Changes:

1. `tests/units/graphdb/test_obo_backends.py` (new)
   Backend-parametrised OBO contract via a `get_request_identity` spy fixture:
   - Delta read through `GraphDBFactory(engine="delta")` binds the forwarded
     user token (OBO) and consults the request identity.
   - Delta read in local mode (`is_databricks_app()` False) keeps the resolved
     SP token — OBO is not applied.
   - Delta build (`for_write=True`) keeps the SP token and never consults the
     identity.
   - Lakebase (`_create_lakebase`) is built from the SP `get_lakebase_auth()`
     result and never reads the request identity.
   - Neo4j (`_create_neo4j`) uses the named Bolt profile's database and never
     reads the request identity.

Modified files:
- tests/units/graphdb/test_obo_backends.py (new)

