## MCP Team gate + fail-closed on the public graph-read handlers

Context:
Part (a) gave the public `/api/v1/*` + `/graphql/*` surface the forwarded
user token for OBO, but the public graph-read handlers still had no Team gate
— the middleware bypasses the session role gate on those prefixes, so
`request.state` carried empty roles and any M2M caller reached graph data.
This closes the gap so MCP-driven reads get the same Viewer+ / admin-bypass /
fail-closed enforcement as Explorer & Graph Chat on the internal routes
(design §MCP: "resolve Team and OBO from the forwarded user headers … fail
closed if those user headers are missing on a data-plane graph or UC route").
Unattended M2M callers with no forwarded user now resolve to `none` → 403.

Changes:

1. `src/api/routers/internal/_graph_access.py`
   Added `assert_public_graph_read(request, domain, settings)`: resolves the
   forwarded user's role for the **target** (query-param / MCP-selected)
   domain via `SettingsService.resolve_domain_role`, stamps it onto
   `request.state`, and delegates to `assert_domain_graph_read` (Viewer+;
   admin bypass; no-op outside App mode).
2. `src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py`
   Threaded `request: Request` into the public graph-read handlers
   (`dt_status`, `dt_stats`, `dt_triples_find`, `dt_triples`,
   `dt_nodes_context`, `dt_nodes_action`, `dt_nodes_virtual_attributes`) and
   call the gate right after `resolve_domain`, before building the store /
   invoking UC. Added a module-level lazy wrapper around the internal gate to
   avoid an import cycle (external Block A is imported by the internal
   package during its own init).
3. `src/back/fastapi/graphql_routes.py`
   Same gate on `graphql_execute` and `graphql_debug` (the graph-reading
   routes); SDL / playground stay open (schema-only, no DB hit). Same lazy
   wrapper to avoid the cycle.
4. `tests/units/api/test_graph_access_gate.py`
   Added `assert_public_graph_read` unit tests (local no-op, non-member 403,
   no-forwarded-user 403, viewer allowed + state stamped, admin bypass) and
   two wiring tests proving `dt_triples_find` and `graphql_execute` invoke the
   gate before touching the store.
5. `tests/units/dtwin/test_digitaltwin_api.py`
   Pass a `request` arg to the direct `dt_triples` / `dt_triples_find` calls
   (gate is a no-op in local test mode).

